{
  "text": "The harbour bridge reopened to traffic on Monday after eight months of repairs to its deck and cables.\n\nThe council's engineer said: \"The cables were replaced one at a time so that the bridge never had to close to pedestrians.\" The work finished two weeks early.\n\nRepairs cost 4.2 million pounds, of which the regional transport fund paid half.",
